From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] quartz/videorenderer: Don't show the window of an
 unconnected renderer.

An application that renders a file into a graph holding a Video
Renderer, then moves the decoder's output to its own filter, may leave
the now unconnected renderer in the graph. The renderer's AutoShow
window was shown on every pause/run regardless, an empty white window
on top of the application's own rendering. Native shows nothing for
an unconnected renderer.

Game impacted: Gunslinger Stratos 2 (Type X3) adds a Video Renderer,
renders the movie file, then reconnects the decoder to a Sample Grabber
and a Null Renderer, keeping the Video Renderer in the graph: the
screen was white for the whole movie (the BYKING intro, the attract
videos), the game's own Direct3D 11 output hidden behind the window.

Show the window only when the input pin is connected.
---
--- a/dlls/quartz/videorenderer.c
+++ b/dlls/quartz/videorenderer.c
@@ -175,7 +175,10 @@
 {
     struct video_renderer *filter = impl_from_strmbase_renderer(iface);
 
-    VideoRenderer_AutoShowWindow(filter);
+    /* An unconnected renderer left in the graph (an application rendering through a
+     * sample grabber instead) shows no window. */
+    if (filter->renderer.sink.pin.peer)
+        VideoRenderer_AutoShowWindow(filter);
 }
 
 static HRESULT video_renderer_connect(struct strmbase_renderer *iface, const AM_MEDIA_TYPE *mt)
